  "changelog": "Initial release of geoskill-fire-weather-index.\n\n- Implements the Canadian Forest Fire Weather Index (FWI) system, recursively calculating FFMC, DMC, DC, ISI, BUI, and FWI from daily meteorological data.\n- Supports both real meteorological raster inputs and synthetic data generation (completely offline).\n- Outputs final-day FWI component stacks, fire danger class rasters, and daily spatial-mean time series in standard formats (GeoTIFF, JSON).\n- Provides clear usage examples and privacy assurances \u2014 all processing is performed locally with no network required.\n- Documentation available in both English and Chinese.",
